  "description": "FAFPIM01 crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C10 H47 Cl1 N5 O27 Sm4 7+,Na1 1+,8(Cl1 O4 1-),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm5 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm6 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm7 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm8 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.827-3.958 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.02-111.37°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Sm4(μ3-OH)4(Gly)5(H2O)11]8+. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 11 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 11 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 8+.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
